# Authentication & Data Access Control with Clerk

All authentication in this project is handled by **Clerk**. Critical security requirement: **Users can ONLY access their own data** and must never be able to access data belonging to other users.

## Authentication Setup

### Required Clerk Imports
```typescript
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
import { currentUser } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation';
```

### Getting Current User ID
```typescript
// In Server Components or API routes
const { userId } = await auth();
if (!userId) {
  redirect('/sign-in');
}

// For user profile information
const user = await currentUser();
```

## Data Access Control Patterns

### MANDATORY: User ID Filtering
**EVERY database query that retrieves user-specific data MUST include user ID filtering:**

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Always filter by userId
const userDecks = await db.select()
  .from(decksTable)
  .where(eq(decksTable.userId, userId));

const userCards = await db.query.cardsTable.findMany({
  where: eq(cardsTable.userId, userId),
});

// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Never query without user filtering
const allDecks = await db.select().from(decksTable);
```

### API Route Security Pattern
All API routes must authenticate and authorize users:

```typescript
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from 'next/server';

export async function GET(request: NextRequest) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  
  if (!userId) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 });
  }

  // Only query user's own data
  const userData = await db.select()
    .from(someTable)
    .where(eq(someTable.userId, userId));
    
  return NextResponse.json(userData);
}
```

### Server Component Security Pattern
```typescript
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation';

export default async function UserDataPage() {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  
  if (!userId) {
    redirect('/sign-in');
  }

  // Always filter by userId
  const userDecks = await db.select()
    .from(decksTable)
    .where(eq(decksTable.userId, userId));

  return (
    <div>
      {/* Render user's data */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Database Schema Requirements

### User ID Column
All user-specific tables MUST include a `userId` column:

```typescript
export const decksTable = pgTable('decks', {
  id: serial('id').primaryKey(),
  userId: text('user_id').notNull(), // REQUIRED for user data isolation
  // ... other columns
});

export const cardsTable = pgTable('cards', {
  id: serial('id').primaryKey(),
  userId: text('user_id').notNull(), // REQUIRED for user data isolation
  deckId: integer('deck_id').references(() => decksTable.id),
  // ... other columns
});
```

## Security Enforcement Rules

### 1. Query Validation
**BEFORE executing any database query, verify:**
- [ ] Does this query involve user-specific data?
- [ ] Is the `userId` filter applied?
- [ ] Can this query potentially return another user's data?

### 2. Parameter Validation
When accepting IDs from client (deck ID, card ID, etc.):

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Verify ownership before using resource ID
async function getUserDeck(deckId: number, userId: string) {
  const deck = await db.query.decksTable.findFirst({
    where: and(
      eq(decksTable.id, deckId),
      eq(decksTable.userId, userId) // CRITICAL: verify ownership
    ),
  });
  
  if (!deck) {
    throw new Error('Deck not found or access denied');
  }
  
  return deck;
}

// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Using resource ID without ownership verification
const deck = await db.query.decksTable.findFirst({
  where: eq(decksTable.id, deckId), // Missing userId check!
});
```

### 3. Insert Operations
Always set userId when creating new records:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Always include userId when creating records
const newDeck = await db.insert(decksTable)
  .values({
    title: deckTitle,
    userId: userId, // REQUIRED
    // ... other fields
  })
  .returning();

// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Creating records without userId
const badDeck = await db.insert(decksTable)
  .values({
    title: deckTitle,
    // Missing userId!
  });
```

### 4. Update/Delete Operations
Always verify ownership before modifying data:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Verify ownership in WHERE clause
await db.update(decksTable)
  .set({ title: newTitle, updatedAt: new Date() })
  .where(and(
    eq(decksTable.id, deckId),
    eq(decksTable.userId, userId) // CRITICAL: verify ownership
  ));

// ✅ CORRECT - Delete with ownership verification
await db.delete(cardsTable)
  .where(and(
    eq(cardsTable.id, cardId),
    eq(cardsTable.userId, userId) // CRITICAL: verify ownership
  ));
```

## Protected Route Patterns

### Page-Level Protection
```typescript
// app/dashboard/page.tsx
import { auth } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation';

export default async function DashboardPage() {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  
  if (!userId) {
    redirect('/sign-in');
  }
  
  // Safe to load user data
  return <DashboardContent userId={userId} />;
}
```

### Middleware Integration
Leverage [middleware.ts](mdc:src/middleware.ts) for route protection:

```typescript
import { clerkMiddleware, createRouteMatcher } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';

const isProtectedRoute = createRouteMatcher([
  '/dashboard(.*)',
  '/flashcards(.*)',
  '/study(.*)',
]);

export default clerkMiddleware(async (auth, req) => {
  if (isProtectedRoute(req)) {
    await auth.protect();
  }
});
```

## Common Security Anti-Patterns

### ❌ NEVER DO THESE:

1. **Skip user authentication checks:**
```typescript
// BAD: No auth check
const data = await db.select().from(decksTable);
```

2. **Query without user filtering:**
```typescript
// BAD: Missing userId filter
const deck = await db.query.decksTable.findFirst({
  where: eq(decksTable.id, deckId),
});
```

3. **Trust client-provided user IDs:**
```typescript
// BAD: Using userId from request body/params
const clientUserId = req.body.userId; // Never trust this!
```

4. **Expose internal IDs without verification:**
```typescript
// BAD: Direct database ID exposure
return NextResponse.json({ internalId: record.id });
```

## Testing Security

### Security Test Checklist
For each new feature, verify:
- [ ] Unauthenticated users are properly redirected
- [ ] Users cannot access other users' data via API manipulation
- [ ] All database queries include proper user filtering
- [ ] Resource ownership is verified before modifications
- [ ] No sensitive data leaks in error messages

### Example Security Test
```typescript
// Verify user data isolation
describe('Data Access Security', () => {
  it('should only return current user data', async () => {
    const user1Data = await getUserDecks(user1Id);
    const user2Data = await getUserDecks(user2Id);
    
    expect(user1Data).not.toContainEqual(
      expect.objectContaining({ userId: user2Id })
    );
  });
});
```

## Critical Security Principle

> **Every database operation involving user data MUST be protected by user ID filtering. No exceptions.**

When in doubt, always err on the side of more restrictive access control rather than less.